  "description": "Two relays serving one site report device.candidates. A device_id and each entity_id are DERIVED from the identity tuple (site, driver, native_id[, entity key]) rather than assigned by either peer, so the device BOTH relays observe resolves to ONE row with one derived id, carrying the relay_id of whichever reported it most recently; the device only one relay observes is its own row. Every derived id is a syntactically valid Canonical ULID (data-model/1 DAT-005a) while a relay_id deliberately is not. The replace each report performs is keyed by device identity and scoped to the reporting relay (REL-111a), so when the second relay stops reporting the shared device it survives and reverts to the relay that still reports it.",
